# Task 26 — Truncating Breadcrumbs

**Category:** Navigation
**Difficulty:** above-average
**Style school:** Corporate SaaS

## The problem

A long breadcrumb trail that must collapse its middle items on small
screens so it doesn't overflow or wrap awkwardly.

## Constraints

- Middle items must be hidden purely via responsive utilities — no JS
  measuring the trail's length or width.

## Key implementation decisions

- The first and last crumbs always stay visible (`Home` and the current
  page), matching the standard breadcrumb truncation convention — the user
  always knows the start and end of the path.
- `$first`/`$last` from the `@for` loop identify the endpoints without any
  manual index math.
- For the middle crumbs, both a `"..."` placeholder (`sm:hidden`) and the
  actual crumb text (`hidden sm:inline`) exist in the DOM at all times;
  Tailwind's responsive variants alone decide which one renders at a given
  screen size — no JavaScript calculates path length or truncates text.

